msgid "When you send a removal request, this site stores what you enter in the form: the link you report, your description and statement, your name as a signature, your email address and, if you give it, your phone number. These details are encrypted. Your IP address is not stored; a one-way code made from it is kept to limit abuse of the form. The people who handle removal requests on this site can read your request to act on it. Your contact details and the request text are deleted %d days after the request is closed. A record of what was done, such as when the request arrived and what was removed, is kept without your contact details. When a request says the person in the image was under 18, the request and the removed files are kept for at least 1 year."
